From da77c2b6a98f546299ef268149518088d86e1ebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:39:51 +0900
Subject: [clang] Code completion loads only matching external names

Qualified and unqualified completion ask the external AST source only for names that can match what was typed (deduction guides and operator names exactly), completion shares the verified full-draft imports and role, and constructor completion emits each canonical overload once.

* perf(clangd): qualified completion loads matching external names

  External namespace completion previously materialized every declaration before
  fuzzy matching. Pass a synchronous consumer predicate to the external source
  and select identifier keys before declaration deserialization. Preserve complete
  ordinary lookup, all overload IDs and nonidentifier traversal names; keep
  external storage for omitted names. The consumer defaults to complete loading.

  Tests exercise real precompiled headers and named modules, fuzzy/empty queries,
  using and inline namespaces, aliases and hiding, merged/overriding lookup tables,
  ordinary lookup after selection, and synchronous source/context scope cleanup.

* perf(clangd): qualified completion filters guides and exact operator names

  External namespace completion still materialized deduction guides and operator
  overloads that could not match the typed query. Match guide template names and
  operator completion spellings before loading their declarations, preserving
  unknown names, ordinary lookup, all overloads and partial external storage.
  Use the actual Sema typed spelling, including operatorco_await.

  Tests compare external and textual completion names, signatures and edits,
  and preserve omitted ordinary lookups and selected overload sets.

* perf(clangd): unqualified completion filters external TU names

  Ordinary-name and expression completion previously enumerated complete external
  translation-unit tables before applying clangd fuzzy matching. Use a borrowed
  completion-only predicate for Scope traversal and external C++ TU names,
  preserving local shadowing, using directives, overloads and ordinary lookup.
  Keep C and empty-pattern behavior unchanged, and preserve partial storage.

  Tests compare PCH and textual unqualified/global completion including aliases,
  inline namespaces, local shadows and bundled overloads, and verify later
  ordinary lookup still loads omitted TU names. No class layout, virtual ABI,
  BMI format or persistent answer cache changes.

* perf(clangd): completion shares verified full-draft imports and role

  The canonical backend returns imports and ordinary-TU proof together for this request. The prefix still receives independent import-free manifest validation. Unknown backends retain conservative queries, and every new request still validates current draft, filesystem observations, command generation and environment.

* fix(sema): constructor completion emits each canonical overload once

  Imported definitions can supply multiple redeclarations of each constructor to one lookup. Constructor expansion now retains one result per canonical overload and updates it with later declaration details, following ordinary completion behavior. Distinct ordinary and template overloads remain. The two-module shared-header regression fixture returns nine constructors before the fix and three after it.
